{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nearestNeighborTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cycle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tours read the simple graph: self-loops are ignored, and each pair of vertices is joined by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its lightest edge (the earliest position on ties), which is the edge the returned ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cycle"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycle.weight(weight)"},{"text":" is the tour’s length. nil below three vertices, before any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other check. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No approximation guarantee in general; within ½(⌈log₂ n⌉ + 1) of the shortest tour when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights satisfy the triangle inequality (Rosenkrantz, Stearns and Lewis, “An analysis","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of several heuristics for the traveling salesman problem”, SIAM Journal on Computing 6,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1977).","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete (every pair of distinct vertices joined); no weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is NaN or infinite."}]}]},{"name":"Complexity","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n²) after O(n + m) to read the edges and weights.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE19nearestNeighborTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"NearestNeighbor.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/NearestNeighbor.swift#L70"},"title":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nearestNeighborTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nearest-neighbour tour from the first vertex (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedy_tsp"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NearestNeighborHeuristicTSP(first)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose default starts at a random vertex): repeatedly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the nearest unvisited vertex, the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order on ties, then back to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start. LEMON’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NearestNeighborTsp"},{"type":"text","text":" shares the name only: it starts from the lightest edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and grows the path at both ends, a different procedure and tour."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/nearestneighbortour(weight:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Walks/documentation/Walks/Cycle":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Cycle","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/walks\/cycle","title":"Cycle","abstract":[{"text":"A cycle: a closed path, at least one edge long, listed without repeating its start (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"simple_cycles","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", petgraph). Vertex i goes to vertex (i + 1) mod ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through edge i, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex or edge position appears twice; a self-loop is a cycle of length 1, two parallel edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one of length 2. It is the witness cycle detection returns.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/nearestNeighborTour(weight:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","kind":"symbol","title":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/nearestneighbortour(weight:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nearest-neighbour tour from the first vertex (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedy_tsp"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NearestNeighborHeuristicTSP(first)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose default starts at a random vertex): repeatedly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the nearest unvisited vertex, the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order on ties, then back to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start. LEMON’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NearestNeighborTsp"},{"type":"text","text":" shares the name only: it starts from the lightest edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and grows the path at both ends, a different procedure and tour."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nearestNeighborTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"pre